---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
import headshot from '../assets/about/headshot.webp';
import wellfleet from '../assets/about/wellfleet.webp';
---

<Layout
  title={`About · ${SITE.name}`}
  description="How Benjamin Reiner got into web development, and the birding and hiking he does outside work."
>
  <h1>About</h1>

  <Figure
    src={headshot}
    width={280}
    photo
    priority
    alt="Benjamin and his partner smiling with their heads together outdoors. He has curly brown hair and wears a black sweatshirt, with binoculars at his chest. She wears a teal, cream, and lavender knit hat. A marsh and a pond are behind them under an overcast sky."
  />

  <section>
    <h2>Work</h2>
    <p>
      My first web work was for First Parish of Sudbury, a congregation of about 150 members. I
      built their main site, which went live just before the COVID-19 pandemic. Once people couldn’t
      meet in person, I built a second site for members, with a BuddyPress forum they used to stay
      in touch.
    </p>
    <p>
      I have a degree in mathematics from Northeastern, where I also did independent research on
      counting square roots of 2×2 matrices over a finite field. I don’t use much of it in my work
      now, but it’s where I learned to work through a problem one step at a time.
    </p>
    <p>
      From March 2024 to August 2026, I was the first dedicated web developer at McGuinness Media
      &amp; Marketing. Besides building and maintaining client sites, I worked with the design,
      media, and client services teams on project planning, SEO, and web design. I also ran
      technical and SEO audits, both for project quotes and as paid evaluations.
    </p>
    <p>
      When we hired a junior developer in January 2026, I became his technical lead. I reviewed his
      code, wrote onboarding docs, and gave him most of the front-end work on new builds, since
      that’s where he was most comfortable. Hiring him is also what led to the starter template on
      the home page. Before I left, I documented the sites I’d built so the team could keep them
      running.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Outside work</h2>
    <p>
      My partner and I are Mass Audubon members, and we hike a lot, mostly at Borderland State Park
      and at Wellfleet Bay Wildlife Sanctuary on Cape Cod. Almost every trip ends up as an eBird
      checklist, and we’ve joined a few bird counts. My favorite bird is the fish crow. It was the
      first bird I identified on my own, and I still love its call.
    </p>

    <Figure
      src={wellfleet}
      alt="A shallow, rippled channel of water curves between a sandy bank and tall green marsh grass, under a pale blue sky with thin clouds. The light is low and warm."
      caption="Wellfleet Bay Wildlife Sanctuary, August 2025."
      photo
      wide
    />

    {/* After the radio exams, change this line to say I’m licensed, and add my call sign. */}
    <p>I’m also studying for my Technician and General amateur radio licenses.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
